# What `gcloud builds submit` must NOT upload into the Cloud Build context.
#
# Without this file gcloud uploads the entire working directory. In CI that
# directory contains the short-lived credentials file that
# google-github-actions/auth writes (gha-creds-*.json), so the OIDC credential
# would be shipped to Cloud Build and land in the build's source archive. Keep
# it out.
#
# Note this is NOT a copy of .dockerignore: cloudbuild.yaml's test step runs
# `npm ci && npm test` against this upload, so tests/, tsconfig and the lock
# file all have to survive. Only the Dockerfile build stage uses .dockerignore.

gha-creds-*.json
*.json.tmp

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
dist
coverage

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
